#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133701 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133885 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ada5d20-89d8-5bc9-9b10-172356be0eb4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Orthogonal Fundamental Subspaces of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "47945f1d-ab72-5fe8-bc2c-43a69480b323" :question/math-academy-id "e-9090" :question/problem "Which of the following subspaces must be orthogonal to $\\text{Col}(A^T)$ for every matrix $A?$\n\nI. $\\text{Null}(A)$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)$\n\nIII. $\\text{Null}(A^T)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A^T)$ is the row space of $A,$ and consists of all linear combinations of the rows of $A.$\n\nIf a vector is orthogonal to every linear combination of the rows of $A,$ it must be orthogonal to each row of $A.$\nBut notice that when pre-multiplying a vector by $A,$ we multiply each row of $A$ by that vector.\nSo, $\\text{Col}(A^T)$ must be orthogonal to the null space of $A,$ which is $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"\n\n**Note:** In general, the four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/de/de22dd5b352e1d5be48f4b6ed3b2a4657ae623c1bd288d3464559758ea334af7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133703 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133887 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a36c7f7-4287-562b-94ea-047b38ede70f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Dimensions of the Four Fundamental Subspaces of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "bb597435-f43e-54de-a219-1af646efcb82" :question/math-academy-id "e-9099" :question/problem "Consider a $8 \\times 6$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A)) = 3,$ then find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}(A^T)).$" :question/worked-solution "The four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/889b83fadd26b377c4dd34143c9b16541630c04e90de3d9b005e7147ead75ad5.png)\n\nIn our case, we are given that $m=8,$ $n=6,$ and $n-r=3.$ \n\nSubstituting $n=6$ into $n-r=3,$ we can find the rank of $A{:}$\n\n$$\n6 - r = 3 \n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nr = 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}({A}^{T})) & =r=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133704 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75e1da77-a5dc-5f78-977e-0d6dae99c97e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Images of the Four Fundamental Subspaces of the Matrix Under Its Action"}] :question/id #uuid "bd1f48b4-8bfc-536d-8145-0effcf44a788" :question/math-academy-id "e-9104" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $m \\times n$ matrix. What is the image of $\\text{Col}(A^T)$ under the action of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Pre-multiplying a vector $\\mathbf{x} \\in \\mathbb{R}^n$ by $A$ gives a linear combination of the columns of $A{:}$\n\n![](images/dc/dc853850b03dd2cf8fcf0168392e3490423725120b6acb55f88028a702d30fa5.svg)\n\nTherefore, the image of $\\mathbb{R}^n$ under the action of $A$ must be $\\text{Col}(A),$ the column space of $A.$\n\nFurthermore, since $\\text{Null}(A)$ is mapped to the zero vector $\\mathbf{0}$ by the definition of the null subspace, the image of its orthogonal complement $\\text{Col}(A^T)$ must be $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nThis can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/8b/8b08bdf79d53f312cabd665bcd4669795bd8851dfb33d5e5db6178bd80b24398.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476953 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75e1da77-a5dc-5f78-977e-0d6dae99c97e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Images of the Four Fundamental Subspaces of the Matrix Under Its Action"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ba3ffed-6f79-5674-89dd-e5713d81b094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476259} {:answer/id #uuid "515a6b57-3dd1-5869-a2e1-3503ded95485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Null}({A}^{T})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476374} {:answer/id #uuid "b217ce6d-e101-5af0-b48d-3de63f2ddbe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476601} {:answer/id #uuid "d22f0a33-a3a6-5ccb-8920-87f9f4d8cda8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}({A}^{T})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476672} {:answer/id #uuid "d5055e1c-9801-5095-928b-f066a25eb52e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b217ce6d-e101-5af0-b48d-3de63f2ddbe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476601} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e95aa0a-fdd3-5df5-8150-f348701b3916" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476777}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bb821d7a-e914-5964-b025-342c273fea77" :question/math-academy-id "q-108924" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $m\\times n$ matrix. What is the image of $\\text{Null}({A}^{T})$ under the action of ${A}^{T}?$" :question/worked-solution "By definition of the null subspace, $\\text{Null}({A}^{T})$ is mapped to the zero vector $0$ under the action of ${A}^{T}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362710 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133885 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ada5d20-89d8-5bc9-9b10-172356be0eb4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Orthogonal Fundamental Subspaces of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a7d2435-e6d8-50bc-9006-6cd7c923b1be" :answer/type {:d