ey "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473648}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9f78c95-881f-537a-b5e6-305264553498" :question/math-academy-id "q-109777" :question/problem "Which of the following subspaces must be orthogonal to $\\text{Col}(A)$ for every matrix $A?$\n- **I.** $\\text{Col}({A}^{T})$\n- **II.** $\\text{Null}({A}^{T})$\n- **III.** $\\text{Null}(A)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ consists of all linear combinations of the columns of $A$, that is, the rows of ${A}^{T}.$\n\nIf a vector is orthogonal to every linear combination of the rows of ${A}^{T},$ it must be orthogonal to each row of ${A}^{T}.$\nBut notice that when pre-multiplying a vector by ${A}^{T},$ we actually multiply each row of ${A}^{T}$ by that vector.\nSo, $\\text{Col}(A)$ must be orthogonal to the left null space of $A,$ which is $\\text{Null}({A}^{T}).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"\n\n**Note:** In general, the four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/de/de22dd5b352e1d5be48f4b6ed3b2a4657ae623c1bd288d3464559758ea334af7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362717 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133885 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ada5d20-89d8-5bc9-9b10-172356be0eb4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Orthogonal Fundamental Subspaces of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b99cf61-4188-5177-9243-e43b4bd470a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468894} {:answer/id #uuid "52f8e72f-d7a5-57c3-963c-58d1ae177c03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b99cf61-4188-5177-9243-e43b4bd470a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468894} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d934aee-1837-5fd6-b7e9-31803fca2c1a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470059} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61cd6959-f3ae-5281-a702-a6f1fbb4b347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468896} {:answer/id #uuid "c766b5e4-f8e9-5807-a6a9-6eea349022f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61cd6959-f3ae-5281-a702-a6f1fbb4b347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468896} :answer-field/id #uuid "e560755c-de37-53f3-abf3-cf0ebd912b36" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470060} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c64afc9-c9f8-5334-bf63-252b9c9011c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468898} {:answer/id #uuid "540b90b9-15b3-5bc0-9d0c-5195e70e08e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "540b90b9-15b3-5bc0-9d0c-5195e70e08e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468899} :answer-field/id #uuid "feb95007-7157-56ac-b69d-8e8b3627d71d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470061}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90aa20cc-7bd4-5b9c-96fe-e3f55743e36c" :question/math-academy-id "q-109781" :question/problem "Which of the following subspaces must be orthogonal to $\\text{Col}({B}^{T})$ for every matrix $B?$\n- **I.** $\\text{Col}(B)$\n- **II.** $\\text{Null}({B}^{T})$\n- **III.** $\\text{Null}(B)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Col}({B}^{T})$ is the row space of $B.$ This consists of all linear combinations of the rows of $B.$\n\nIf a vector is orthogonal to every linear combination of the rows of $B,$ it must be orthogonal to each row of $B.$\nBut notice that when pre-multiplying a vector by $B,$ we actually multiply each row of $B$ by that vector.\nSo, $\\text{Col}({B}^{T})$ must be orthogonal to the null space of $B,$ which is $\\text{Null}(B).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"\n\n**Note:** In general, the four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/18/18713ed3d103ca0a02d74cede1e6448012e0aa28a2df804d41cfb277589a0158.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133887 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a36c7f7-4287-562b-94ea-047b38ede70f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Dimensions of the Four Fundamental Subspaces of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35f644fb-8086-555f-b786-602d1979ce61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362732} {:answer/id #uuid "bea4a0b0-d1b5-5839-b044-8108d6b9ddd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362733} {:answer/id #uuid "5565d328-aa38-5f70-98e1-4235e6b2083d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362734} {:answer/id #uuid "ddf71678-271a-5c3f-81ec-cb9596b621d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362735} {:answer/id #uuid "9d8d1290-ea1d-567f-8d0b-a0f233dca5dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bea4a0b0-d1b5-5839-b044-8108d6b9ddd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362733} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff003ae2-5c05-524e-9932-2c06214cec61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aa262e05-5582-5f00-bdc8-007681456bff" :question/math-academy-id "q-109845" :question/problem "Consider a $4\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))=1,$ then $\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}({A}^{T}))=$" :question/worked-solution "The four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/889b83fadd26b377c4dd34143c9b16541630c04e90de3d9b005e7147ead75ad5.png)\n\nIn our case, we are given that $m=4,$ $n=3,$ and $n-r=1.$ \n\nSubstituting $n=3$ into $n-r=1,$ we can find the rank of $A:$\n\n$$\n(3)-r=1\\,⟹\\,r=2\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}({A}^{T})) & =r=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407243 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133887 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a36c7f7-4287-562b-94ea-047b38ede70f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Dimensions of the Four Fundamental Subspaces of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "166f24b3-2b33-5589-9ba5-efd73efdf696" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407215} {:answer/id #uuid "794d7c6a-4727-5c98-8506-efa641e24334" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407222} {:answer/id #uuid "c4f31e2f-2172-581c-b46f-338027d98c9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407229} {:answer/id #uuid "de4a68e5-c938-5191-8ef4-522e158bedb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407233} {:answer/id #uuid "f4d32fbe-6d2e-5aca-9070-ed1ab0efc4fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4f31e2f-2172-581c-b46f-338027d98c9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407229} :answer-field/id #uuid "077cd26a-5956-5d07-8539-e101ab53d7f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407238}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5d75070f-88dd-5b20-8fec-c1f3c6de013c" :question/math-academy-id "q-109846" :question/problem "Consider a $5\\times 4$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}({A}^{T}))=3,$ then $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))=$" :question/worked-solution "The four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/889b83fadd26b377c4dd34143c9b16541630c04e90de3d9b005e7147ead75ad5.png)\n\nIn our case, we are given that $m=5,$ $n=4,$ and $r=3.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A)) & =n-r=4-3=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134076 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133887 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a36c7f7-4287-562b-94ea-047b38ede70f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Dimensions of the Four Fundamental Subspaces of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1abcc03-91d1-552b-9d4d-9a115b7162b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362738} {:answer/id #uuid "c60509e5-818a-5e5e-b197-6af69774dd36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362739} {:answer/id #uuid "f75117f4-5157-5a16-8cc6-ba4f53bf01b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362740} {:answer/id #uuid "12667677-285f-5967-a229-9a31385011dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362741} {:answer/id #uuid "74b909d7-4810-52a5-b17e-ba23c831d0b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1abcc03-91d1-552b-9d4d-9a115b7162b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362738} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c5d07ae-1027-53fa-a3de-70f4fa5a1296" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "485e3060-5691-5e86-bcb1-ec2efd550199" :question/math-academy-id "q-109847" :question/problem "Consider a $7\\times 5$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}(A))=4,$ then $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}({A}^{T}))=$" :question/worked-solution "The four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/889b83fadd26b377c4dd34143c9b16541630c04e90de3d9b005e7147ead75ad5.png)\n\nIn our case, we are given that $m=7,$ $n=5,$ and $r=4.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}({A}^{T})) & =m-r=7-4=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476888 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133885 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ada5d20-89d8-5bc9-9b10-172356be0eb4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Orthogonal Fundamental Subspaces of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18841c85-4169-5e21-aa60-7f9429a69ea9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476243} {:answer/id #uuid "32eb844c-ce40-54f8-8182-8bdb52ef41a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476316} {:answer/id #uuid "be8b7e98-b032-5486-9065-1ba9e55cd64e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476636} {:answer/id #uuid "c719959b-438d-5216-87e0-1e590c4937dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476652} {:answer/id #uuid "e3f9aeac-42a7-57b9-961a-8f9b80d6c9b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32eb844c-ce40-54f8-8182-8bdb52ef41a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476316} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef854973-f40e-54d0-8398-b5ed45b6afdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476861}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3930016a-7426-5deb-b0f0-c2074d3a1ffd" :question/math-academy-id "q-109856" :question/problem "Which of the following subspaces must be orthogonal to $\\text{Null}(A+B)$ for all compatible matrices $A$ and $B?$\n\nI. $\\text{Null}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})$\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}(A+B)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Null}(A+B)$ contains all vectors that, when pre-multiplied by $A+B,$ result in the zero-vector $0.$ \n\nWhen pre-multiplying a vector by $A+B,$ we actually multiply each row of $A+B$ by that vector. So, $\\text{Null}(A+B)$ must be orthogonal to the row space of $A+B,$ which is $\\text{Col}((A+B)^{T})=\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T}).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"\n\n**Note:** In general, the four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/de/de22dd5b352e1d5be48f4b6ed3b2a4657ae623c1bd288d3464559758ea334af7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476895 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133885 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ada5d20-89d8-5bc9-9b10-172356be0eb4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Orthogonal Fundamental Subspaces of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c6d4e70-0448-5ab5-9f2d-ce038f339c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476265} {:answer/id #uuid "7cd9368f-9feb-504f-a71d-cd5bb34f56ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476479} {:answer/id #uuid "ae6f1a68-607c-5b44-a425-625c20d52a6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476589} {:answer/id #uuid "e41a1e37-3b17-5fc8-8508-7b738b3b3074" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476710} {:answer/id #uuid "f85e9333-5d0e-542b-837b-a916ca56e2ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae6f1a68-607c-5b44-a425-625c20d52a6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476589} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f9bb4ab-702b-5516-8021-d3e236ee68e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476778}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4d68ce86-72b3-53d7-b424-c8c3717fc180" :question/math-academy-id "q-109857" :question/problem "Which of the following subspaces must be orthogonal to $\\text{Null}({X}^{T}{Y}^{T})$ for all compatible matrices $X$ and $Y?$\n\nI. $\\text{Null}(YX)$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}({X}^{T}{Y}^{T})$\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}(YX)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{Null}({X}^{T}{Y}^{T})$ contains all vectors that, when pre-multiplied by ${X}^{T}{Y}^{T},$ result in the zero-vector $0.$ \n\nWhen pre-multiplying a vector by ${X}^{T}{Y}^{T},$ we actually multiply each row of ${X}^{T}{Y}^{T}$ by that vector. So, $\\text{Null}({X}^{T}{Y}^{T})$ must be orthogonal to the row space of ${X}^{T}{Y}^{T},$ which is $\\text{Col}(({X}^{T}{Y}^{T})^{T})=\\text{Col}(YX).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"\n\n**Note:** In general, the four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/de/de22dd5b352e1d5be48f4b6ed3b2a4657ae623c1bd288d3464559758ea334af7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380573 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75e1da77-a5dc-5f78-977e-0d6dae99c97e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Images of the Four Fundamental Subspaces of the Matrix Under Its Action"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7716a75-0eea-5e7d-8387-1aa17c566b26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Null}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380575} {:answer/id #uuid "c669296d-1bdf-527a-aa02-77c5f5fc6df1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380576} {:answer/id #uuid "9fbdf937-1217-53c1-8187-c84c2557e123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380577} {:answer/id #uuid "2c7651c9-51f8-5028-9d93-a70283285549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380578} {:answer/id #uuid "d3bd6a53-d027-5e1c-b16c-738508b17ed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c669296d-1bdf-527a-aa02-77c5f5fc6df1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380576} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2aaa4ba-aa2b-5c63-98dd-d56973b99ffc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380574}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "944155a1-9519-5409-8508-216f9904bbe8" :question/math-academy-id "q-109859" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $7\\times 5$ matrix. What is the image of ${R}^{5}$ under the action of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Pre-multiplying a vector $x\\in {R}^{5}$ by $A$ gives a linear combination of the columns of $A:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} & {a}_{4} & {a}_{5} \\\\ | & | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{5}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {a}_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {a}_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {a}_{3} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{4}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {a}_{4} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{5}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {a}_{5} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{5}$ under the action of $A$ must be $\\text{Col}(A),$ the column space of $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407247 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75e1da77-a5dc-5f78-977e-0d6dae99c97e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Images of the Four Fundamental Subspaces of the Matrix Under Its Action"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d3a4ec2-bd1c-569f-bc25-a735fbf6e8f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407213} {:answer/id #uuid "4624e774-8f8e-50d7-922a-9f2511cb84dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Null}(AB)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407218} {:answer/id #uuid "ab8461c5-2db5-555b-98b8-ef3d5aadb4ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}({B}^{T}{A}^{T})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407225} {:answer/id #uuid "ca1a752d-a1b9-5c75-a6eb-005f23fda936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Null}({B}^{T}{A}^{T})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407230} {:answer/id #uuid "cafe991c-8437-5728-ad05-fe57c0cef2d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}(AB)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cafe991c-8437-5728-ad05-fe57c0cef2d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}(AB)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407231} :answer-field/id #uuid "a14d9fc2-b7d8-5af8-b07b-319f63dc6ba1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "de769de3-3ab7-5536-ae28-2dcbd744b48f" :question/math-academy-id "q-109861" :question/problem "Let $A$ and $B$ be $m\\times p$ and $p\\times n$ matrices, respectively. What is the image of $\\text{Col}({B}^{T}\\,{A}^{T})$ under the action of $AB?$" :question/worked-solution "Pre-multiplying a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ by $AB$ gives a linear combination of the columns of $AB:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & ⋯ & | \\\\ (ab)_{1} & (ab)_{2} & ⋯ & (ab)_{n} \\\\ | & | & ⋯ & |\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{AB}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (ab)_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (ab)_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+⋯+{x}_{n}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (ab)_{n} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{n}$ under the action of $AB$ must be $\\text{Col}(AB),$ the column space of $AB.$\n\nFurthermore, since $\\text{Null}(AB)$ is mapped to the zero vector $0$ by the definition of the null subspace, the image of its orthogonal complement $\\text{Col}((AB)^{T})=\\text{Col}({B}^{T}\\,{A}^{T})$ must be $\\text{Col}(AB).$\n\nThis can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/885bf8a3061f93ad400897a7273ffe4157d22dee20b8e4ee7ebb982b1c4319bb.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476920 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75e1da77-a5dc-5f78-977e-0d6dae99c97e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Images of the Four Fundamental Subspaces of the Matrix Under Its Action"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31717965-8188-5614-b5bd-dd4dd34c9a60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476312} {:answer/id #uuid "403bca0a-677d-50cb-b10a-cd4b757641d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476344} {:answer/id #uuid "5d1065b6-e4be-5ce4-9c44-479b99525728" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476411} {:answer/id #uuid "727a6de3-6a1e-54e5-a473-aa66302930e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Null}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476464} {:answer/id #uuid "a6f3fa59-0a17-562e-a0aa-5241c84a1cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "403bca0a-677d-50cb-b10a-cd4b757641d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476344} :answer-field/id #uuid "eeeef6de-d8de-527e-81b4-5538bfa583c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476860}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "814b73ba-57d5-52a9-8c36-0c9f156faa4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-109863" :question/problem "Let $A$ and $B$ be $m\\times n$ matrices. What is the image of ${R}^{m}$ under the action of ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}$ is a $n\\times m$ matrix.\n\nNow, pre-multiplying a vector $x\\in {R}^{m}$ by ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}$ gives a linear combination of the columns of ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & ⋯ & | \\\\ ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{1} & ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{2} & ⋯ & ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{m} \\\\ | & | & ⋯ & |\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{T}+{B}^{T}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{m}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+⋯+{x}_{m}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{m} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{m}$ under the action of ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}$ must be $\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T}),$ the row space of $A+B.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397950 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75e1da77-a5dc-5f78-977e-0d6dae99c97e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Images of the Four Fundamental Subspaces of the Matrix Under Its Action"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4a3e2b6-7b29-5528-96b5-7573a1aadd7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Null}(A+B)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397952} {:answer/id #uuid "4bbf2858-8656-5cf8-89b6-f411004b18f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397953} {:answer/id #uuid "343e1966-1342-5cc5-9cd1-08091ba5d293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Null}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397954} {:answer/id #uuid "ce963992-d45b-5324-bb97-8def95d4a96a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}(A+B)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397955} {:answer/id #uuid "bd6b2f33-a870-578b-9b44-33252827ba71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce963992-d45b-5324-bb97-8def95d4a96a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}(A+B)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397955} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f937f66-6317-5bbf-a1a5-7a91aa314279" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397951}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3b884b20-b24f-567b-b7d3-aeaaf2084dca" :question/math-academy-id "q-109865" :question/problem "Let $A$ and $B$ be $m\\times n$ matrices. What is the image of $\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})$ under the action of $A+B?$" :question/worked-solution "Pre-multiplying a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ by $A+B$ gives a linear combination of the columns of $A+B:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & ⋯ & | \\\\ (a+b)_{1} & (a+b)_{2} & ⋯ & (a+b)_{n} \\\\ | & | & ⋯ & |\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A+B}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (a+b)_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (a+b)_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+⋯+{x}_{n}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (a+b)_{n} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{n}$ under the action of $A+B$ must be $\\text{Col}(A+B),$ the column space of $A+B.$\n\nFurthermore, since $\\text{Null}(A+B)$ is mapped to the zero vector $0$ by the definition of the null subspace, the image of its orthogonal complement $\\text{Col}((A+B)^{T})=\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})$ must be $\\text{Col}(A+B).$\n\nThis can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/02/02a739d8888f2b46b81075218693e6b2cc87e3c5b81b522abfc9246dcd7c870d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476871 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133887 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a36c7f7-4287-562b-94ea-047b38ede70f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Dimensions of the Four Fundamental Subspaces of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0da496da-39d4-5467-8ef4-2d29819ae5dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476225} {:answer/id #uuid "49072a3f-f9fa-5790-946c-8dd612dd63c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476357} {:answer/id #uuid "5a37659d-ffc5-541b-9c9c-a62a346075cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476402} {:answer/id #uuid "62e07be3-aeb6-5604-a439-fca42c4eb3c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476426} {:answer/id #uuid "ecd87db2-d45d-51ab-9b08-3ac6a96d531d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49072a3f-f9fa-5790-946c-8dd612dd63c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476357} :answer-field/id #uuid "19162954-e902-549b-b60d-14561c8bf06c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476769}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0027448d-1eb1-5ed1-bd4f-f6f90763ed8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-109872" :question/problem "Consider a $7\\times 8$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}(A))=4,$ then $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))=$" :question/worked-solution "The four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/889b83fadd26b377c4dd34143c9b16541630c04e90de3d9b005e7147ead75ad5.png)\n\nIn our case, we are given that $m=7,$ $n=8,$ and $r=4.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A)) & =n-r=8-4=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380587 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133887 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a36c7f7-4287-562b-94ea-047b38ede70f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Dimensions of the Four Fundamental Subspaces of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a122686f-5678-58d1-8a1c-486568c84f7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380589} {:answer/id #uuid "879a3efb-b935-5885-b811-59d864294bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380590} {:answer/id #uuid "aa17be9f-3cd5-594e-9da4-6ced97082d68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380591} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c3b167-1ee9-5ae9-9508-c95b81f0d0fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380592} {:answer/id #uuid "88312b9d-d971-513f-98d9-cd5c7226ba2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "879a3efb-b935-5885-b811-59d864294bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380590} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9acb45d-34b0-5c35-8602-902834ee8788" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380588}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d2ae3acf-040a-593b-a06c-a21a12ea38ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-109878" :question/problem "Consider a $9\\times 4$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}(A))=2,$ then $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}({A}^{T}))=$" :question/worked-solution "The four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/889b83fadd26b377c4dd34143c9b16541630c04e90de3d9b005e7147ead75ad5.png)\n\nIn our case, we are given that $m=9,$ $n=4,$ and $r=2.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}({A}^{T})) & =m-r=9-2=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
